  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expansion of the Familias en Accin Conditional Cash Transfer Program  Phase II</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Programa de Subsidios Condicionados, Familias en Accin - Fase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El fin del programa es contribuir con la estrategia del GCO para reducirla pobreza y la pobreza extrema en el mediano plazo, incrementandotemporalmente el consumo, as como el nivel de capital humano, de al menos 1,5milln de familias de escasos recursos, mediante el apoyo a la expansin de FA.El objetivo general de esta segunda fase del programa, es contribuir al aumentodel ingreso y la promocin de la acumulacin de capital humano de las familiasque viven en situacin de pobreza (SISBEN I y desplazados). Los objetivosespecficos son: (i) complementar el ingreso de las familias pobres urbanas connios menores de 18 aos; (ii) promover la formacin de capital humano a travsdel aumento del uso de servicios de desarrollo infantil temprano, educacin ysalud; (iii) mejorar la calidad del programa a travs del fortalecimiento continuode sus herramientas de gestin tcnica; y (iv) ajustar el diseo de Familias enAccin conforme a los resultados de la agenda de evaluacin en curso.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the program is to contribute to the Colombian governments strategy of reducing poverty and extreme poverty in the medium term by temporarily increasing consumption and raising the level of human capital for at least 1.5 million poor families through support for the expansion of Familias en Accin. The overall objective of this second phase of the program is to help to raise income and promote human capital accumulation in families living in poverty (SISBEN I and displaced persons). The specific objectives are: (i) to supplement the income of poor urban families with children under 18 years; (ii) to promote human capital formation by increasing the use of early childhood development, educational, and health care services; (iii) to improve program quality through continued strengthening of its technical management tools; and (iv) to modify the design of Familias en Accin in accordance with the findings of the evaluation agenda under way.</narrative>
  </description>
